    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="0719" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg621"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5703a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 852</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-08-26">August 26, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department’s records indicate that the
                    Chinese Government has failed, since August 17, 1931, to effect any payments in
                    connection with the claims awarded American claimants as a result of the Nanking
                    incident of March 24, 1927.<anchor n="74" xml:id="d696-f1"/> In this connection
                    the Department requests that you bring this matter to the attention of the
                    appropriate authorities of the Chinese Government with a view to obtaining
                    payment, without further delay, of the sums which are now in default.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R. Castle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
